class:: HarmonicChange
summary:: Causal tonal-centroid change magnitude
categories:: UGens>Analysis>Tonal
related:: Guides/MIR2, Classes/HPCP, Classes/HarmonicPeaks

description::
Applies the Harte, Sandler and Gasser (2006) tonal-centroid transform and computes Euclidean distance between the current centroid and the centroid two accepted observations earlier. This is the centred harmonic-change difference reported one observation late, after optional causal exponential smoothing. The first two observations output zero. Values occur on accepted trigger blocks; other blocks output zero. Tonal-centroid distance detects changes in pitch-class geometry and can also respond to changing timbre or noise.



classmethods::
method:: kr
argument:: chroma
A C-first Array of 12, 24, 36, or 120 nonnegative pitch-class values. Higher resolutions fold to nearest semitones where a twelve-class representation is required.

argument:: smooth
Causal exponential smoothing time in seconds, zero disables. Time follows the actual interval between trigger updates.

argument:: trig
A positive value processes this control block. For FFT-derived features pass chain >= 0 so each analysis frame is used once; default 1 processes each control block.

returns::
Nonnegative six-dimensional Euclidean distance, delayed by one observation relative to the centred difference.

examples::
HarmonicChange detects harmonic transitions by calculating 6D Euclidean distance in Tonnetz space between consecutive observations. Harmonic chord progressions produce prominent distance spikes upon new chord arrivals. In this example, detected harmonic transitions trigger a delicate bell chime on chord changes. An interactive code::MIR2GUI.scope:: displays real-time harmonic change distance.
code::
(
s.waitForBoot({
    var path = MIR2GUI.soundPath("piano-chords.wav");
    ~mir2Buffer = if(path.notNil) { Buffer.read(s, path) } { nil };
    ~mir2Bus = Bus.control(s, 1);
    s.sync;
    ~mir2Example = {
        var source = if(~mir2Buffer.notNil) {
            PlayBuf.ar(1, ~mir2Buffer, BufRateScale.kr(~mir2Buffer), loop: 1)
        } {
            // Synthetic chords fallback
            Mix.ar(SinOsc.ar([261.63, 329.63, 392.00, 523.25] * LFNoise0.kr(0.5).range(1, 1.25))) * 0.15
        };
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar(0);

        var chain = FFT(LocalBuf(2048), source, 0.25);
        var chroma = HPCP.kr(chain, size: 12, harmonics: 2, normalize: \max, fftSize: 2048);
        var change = HarmonicChange.kr(chroma, smooth: 0.05, trig: chain >= 0);
        var chgTrig = (change > 0.15).lag(0.01, 0.08);
        var chime = Ringz.ar(Decay2.ar(K2A.ar(chgTrig), 0.002, 0.05) * 0.05, 2200, 0.3) * 0.3;
        var sound = (source * 0.25 ! 2) + (chime ! 2);

        if(~mir2Bus.notNil) { Out.kr(~mir2Bus, change.clip(0, 1)) };
        sound * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.2)
    }.play;

    ~mir2GUI = MIR2GUI.scope("Harmonic Change", ~mir2Bus, 0.0, 1.0, "dist");
});
)
::
code::
(
~mir2Example.free;
if(~mir2GUI.notNil) { ~mir2GUI.close };
if(~mir2Bus.notNil) { ~mir2Bus.free };
if(~mir2Buffer.notNil) { ~mir2Buffer.free };
)
::

